%I A399679 #21 Sep 29 2026 23:38:12
%S A399679 1,1,8,65,841,56428
%N A399679 Number of nonisomorphic strong doppelsemigroups of order n.
%C A399679 A doppelsemigroup is an algebraic structure (D,-|,|-) consisting of a set D equipped with two associative binary operations -| and |- satisfying the following axioms: (x-|y)|-z=x-|(y|-z) and (x|-y)-|z=x|-(y-|z).
%C A399679 A doppelsemigroup (D,-|,|-) is called strong when the axiom x-|(y|-z)=x|-(y-|z) holds.
%H A399679 V.M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://doi.org/10.15421/242602">Note on the number of doppelsemigroups of small order</a>, Res. Math. 34(1) (2026), 16-33.
%H A399679 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22642383">Lists of All Pairwise Nonisomorphic Strong Doppelsemigroups of Orders up to 5</a>.
%H A399679 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://gist.github.com/vgavrylkiv/bdf06def09430abfb06a4c16ee0baa95">Python code for computing nonisomorphic doppelsemigroups</a>.
%e A399679 For n = 2, there are exactly 8 nonisomorphic strong doppelsemigroups (D,-|,|-) on the set D={0,1}. Rows and columns are ordered as 0,1. The Cayley tables of all eight doppelsemigroups are listed below.
%e A399679 Doppelsemigroup #1:
%e A399679   -|:   |-:
%e A399679   0 0   0 0
%e A399679   0 0   0 0
%e A399679 Doppelsemigroup #2:
%e A399679   -|:   |-:
%e A399679   0 0   0 0
%e A399679   0 0   0 1
%e A399679 Doppelsemigroup #3:
%e A399679   -|:   |-:
%e A399679   0 1   0 1
%e A399679   1 0   1 0
%e A399679 Doppelsemigroup #4:
%e A399679   -|:   |-:
%e A399679   0 1   1 0
%e A399679   1 0   0 1
%e A399679 Doppelsemigroup #5:
%e A399679   -|:   |-:
%e A399679   0 0   0 0
%e A399679   0 1   0 0
%e A399679 Doppelsemigroup #6:
%e A399679   -|:   |-:
%e A399679   0 0   0 0
%e A399679   0 1   0 1
%e A399679 Doppelsemigroup #7:
%e A399679   -|:   |-:
%e A399679   0 0   0 0
%e A399679   1 1   1 1
%e A399679 Doppelsemigroup #8:
%e A399679   -|:   |-:
%e A399679   0 1   0 1
%e A399679   0 1   0 1
